  "interpretation": [
    "The shared case uses 600 roles with the same inline policy and trust policy. Complete IAM findings, graph and principal projection use 22.77% less CPU and 45.10% lower peak traced allocations; wall time falls 22.83%.",
    "Repeated trust policies with otherwise unique inline policies save 4.87% CPU for percent-encoded inputs and 2.08% peak allocations. JSON inputs save 2.07% peak allocations but use 1.37% more CPU in this run.",
    "Unique-policy control uses 1.85% less CPU after adaptive admission, with effectively unchanged allocation peak. The initial cache without adaptive admission cost 5.58% more CPU on this control; both trials are retained.",
    "Already-decoded control uses 2.62% more CPU (~15.7ms for 600 roles); allocations are essentially unchanged. The cache benefit depends on repeated encoded policies and is not a universal speedup.",
    "Each mode has 6 interleaved runs per variant, separate tracing runs, exact predecessor parser function and fresh scan contexts. Setup, fingerprints and native cold initialization are excluded.",
    "These are synthetic complete offline IAM-stage measurements, not whole-scan timings, live network savings or process RSS. Cache charge is conservative admission accounting, not a process-memory limit."
  ],
